export const metaTitle = "Airfield Signs: Runway & Taxiway Signage Guide | Jetsys Defence";
export const metaDescription = "Explore airfield signs, runway and taxiway guidance, sign colours and illumination. Compare specifications and learn what to check when selecting signage for your airfield.";

export const introduction = [
  "At a taxiway junction, a flight crew may need to identify its current position, find the next turn and recognise a runway holding position in quick succession. Airfield signs give crews and authorised vehicle drivers distinct visual cues for each of those decisions. Together with surface markings, lighting and local operating instructions, they help people move through the aerodrome without confusing a route indication with a restriction.",
  "Airfield signs convey mandatory instructions or provide information such as location, direction and destination. The colour scheme helps identify the function before the legend is read. A runway holding sign, a taxiway location panel and an exit arrow may appear within the same stretch of pavement, but each answers a different question. Their design and placement have to work together.",
  "This guide is for aerodrome operators, consultants, contractors and maintenance teams specifying new signs or replacing installed equipment. Jetsys Defence lists an internally illuminated taxiway guidance sign in its Runway Spares catalogue. Signage forms part of the wider airfield lighting and visual guidance system.",
];

