            answer: "Airfield signs are visual aids that give instructions or guidance to flight crews and authorised vehicle drivers on and around an aerodrome’s movement area. They identify routes, locations, destinations and points where restrictions apply. The colour and format help the reader recognise the sign family before reading its full legend.",
